{"id": "mm7105a1", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011Cgg9uTTasyR5bSJJjb5hN", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 11170, "output": 3260}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"id\": \"mm7105a1\", \"data_focus\": {\"v\": \"yes\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"the prevalence of reporting fair/poor physical health was significantly higher in medium/small urban (31.1%), metro-adjacent rural (40.2%), and remote rural (34.0%) counties\"}, {\"loc\": \"summary\", \"q\": \"During 2021, working-aged adults in small/medium urban counties and rural counties reported worse physical health compared with residents of large urban counties.\"}]}, \"outcome_types\": [{\"v\": \"binary/categorical\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"the prevalence of reporting fair/poor physical health was significantly higher\"}]}], \"analytic_depth\": [{\"v\": \"comparison\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"table 2\", \"q\": \"Metro-adjacent rural | 687 | 40.2 | <0.001\"}]}, {\"v\": \"stratified/adjusted\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Logistic regression analyses predicting self-reported fair/poor physical health with clustered standard errors for states\"}]}], \"study_design\": [{\"v\": \"cross-sectional\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"NWS is a national, cross-sectional, web-based survey of U.S. adults aged 18–64 years\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Logistic regression analyses predicting self-reported fair/poor physical health with clustered standard errors for states were used to calculate predicted probabilities\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"All analyses were weighted with the poststratification weight and conducted using SAS software (version 9.4; SAS Institute).\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Poststratification demographic weights were used to allow generalizability to the broader U.S. working-aged population.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Step